 256:Core/Src/flash.c **** /**
 257:Core/Src/flash.c ****  * @brief  Configures the MX25L51245G flash memory for high-speed Quad I/O operation.
 258:Core/Src/flash.c ****  * @note   This sequence performs three critical steps:
 259:Core/Src/flash.c ****  * 1. Enables 32-bit (4-byte) addressing mode to access the full 512Mb range.
 260:Core/Src/flash.c ****  * 2. Sets the Quad Enable (QE) bit in the Status/Configuration registers.
 261:Core/Src/flash.c ****  * 3. Ensures proper write synchronization using Flash_WaitWhileBusy().
 262:Core/Src/flash.c ****  * * @details The MX25L51245G requires a 16-bit write (Status Reg + Config Reg) to 
 263:Core/Src/flash.c ****  * persistently enable Quad Mode via the QE bit (Bit 6 of Status Register).
 264:Core/Src/flash.c ****  * InstructionMode is set to 1-Line for initial configuration as the 
 265:Core/Src/flash.c ****  * device boots in standard SPI mode.
 266:Core/Src/flash.c ****  * * @param  None
 267:Core/Src/flash.c ****  * @retval None
 268:Core/Src/flash.c ****  */
